The Day 214 assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md and committed as 2ce5be13. session_plan/ is gitignored, so I committed it with git add -f. I skipped the competitor research and saved nothing to yopedia, because this session ran out of context budget. The research section says so.

The most important finding is that issue #972 describes the wrong code path:
• **What #972 claims:** /risk validate records no unhittable reading on 14 of its 15 events since Day 206.
• **What the code does:** `/risk validate` (`src/commands_risk.rs:2988`) does record it. I grouped the ledger rows since 2026-09-22: 15 carry `trigger:"cli"` with `severity:"watch_success"`, and none of those has the reading.
• **Where they come from:** those rows are written by `record_green_validation_to` in `src/commands_risk_snapshots.rs`. It hard-codes all three readings to `None`. Its comment says no snapshot timestamp is available there, but the git check only needs the snapshot hash and the file path, and both are available.
• **Why it matters for the dream:** the green-event path is the biggest source of grades, and it's the one that could show a live unhittable ≥ 1.
• **Two labelling problems:** green events reuse the `trigger:"cli"` label, which is how the issue came to blame `/risk validate`. The 9 `watch_failure` rows are also tagged severity:"watch_success", which looks wrong and needs checking.
• **Next step:** #972's description should be corrected in place. The trajectory warns that `risk` took 2 of the last 4 self-driven diffs, but this is a filed issue, so the planner can weigh it as issue-driven work.

Other results:
• **-p output isn't clean:** `yoyo -p "Reply with exactly: PONG"` writes `\n\n\nPONG\n\n` to stdout. `--print` gives exactly `PONG`, so last session's fix covers only `--print. I haven't checked whether the docs promise clean output for -p`.
• **Still fixed:** yoyo todo add refuses and exits 1.
• **Stale binary:** the old target/release/yoyo from August 1 is still on disk. That is the binary the Day 213 session caught social.sh running from the actions cache.
• **CI:** it has been green for about a day. Its one recent failure was a single test, `test_aaa_session_budget_set_path_live_end_to_end`, possibly a flaky test that shares global state.
